  "label": "Rural Farmers Stereotype",
  "description": "The meme relies on the stereotype that farmers, especially those in rural or developing regions, are either primitive, uneducated, or not capable of raising healthy animals. The text 'when you're a good farmer' implies that such success is rare or exceptional, which may be interpreted as condescending or dismissive of the everyday labor of farmers. This stereotype is not visible in the image but is required to understand the potential underlying message or intent of the meme.",
